---
/**
 * /budgeting
 *
 * Angle: Budget-focused users, expense trackers, YNAB-style envelope budgeters
 * Audience: People who want structured budgeting with expense tracking
 * Intent: "I want to budget my money and track my spending"
 *
 * Target Keywords (High Volume):
 * - budgeting app (100K-1M)
 * - budget app (100K-1M)
 * - budget planner (10K-100K)
 * - expense tracking (1K-10K)
 * - envelope budgeting (1K-10K)
 * - zero based budgeting (10K-100K)
 * - spending tracker (1K-10K)
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages, APP_URL, SITE_URL } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.budgetingApp;

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "How can I stop overspending on things I don't really need?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "The trick is catching overspending before it becomes a pattern. Set category limits that reflect what you actually want to spend, not what you think you should spend. When you see your dining-out category at €180/€200 by the 20th of the month, that visual feedback creates a natural pause. Track spending as it happens so you know what's left, and suddenly that impulse purchase competes with your other priorities. Financial awareness is what changes spending habits."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "I'm new to budgeting. Where do I start?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Start with one month. Log your income, create spending categories that match your actual life (rent, groceries, transport, fun money), and assign every dollar until you hit zero unassigned. Use starter templates if you need guidance. Then track spending for 30 days—just a few minutes daily. Don't aim for perfection; aim for awareness. After one month, you'll see your real patterns, and month two gets easier. Budgeting for beginners is about building the habit first, optimizing later. For more on the basics, see our personal finance guide."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "What's the difference between a spending plan and a budget?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "A budget is often backward-looking: what you spent last month. A spending plan is forward-looking: what you're going to spend this month and why. Zero-based budgeting combines both. You plan at the start (spending plan), then track against that plan (budget management) as the month unfolds. The best budget software turns your plan into a live tracker so you're always comparing intention against reality."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "Can budgeting help if I'm living paycheck to paycheck?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Yes. Zero-based budgeting works especially well when money is tight because every dollar gets a specific job before you spend it. Start by budgeting what you have right now, not what you hope to earn next month. Assign money to must-pay bills first, then essentials, then whatever's left. Envelope budgeting shows you exactly what's available without touching money that's already allocated. Seeing your cashflow clearly is often the first step to breaking the cycle."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "Do I really need a budget if I'm not struggling with money?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Even if you're not in financial trouble, a budget shows you opportunities you're missing. Where could you cut €100/month without noticing? Which spending categories are creeping up? How much could you actually save or invest if you were intentional? A spending plan isn't about fixing problems—it's about optimizing what's already working. People with healthy finances often benefit most from budget management because they have room to make strategic choices. Tracking monthly spending turns vague financial goals into concrete actions."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
  ogImage={meta.ogImage}
  keywords={meta.keywords}
>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      name: meta.title,
      description: meta.description,
      url: `${SITE_URL}/${meta.slug}`,
    })}
  </script>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE_URL },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Budgeting', item: `${SITE_URL}/${meta.slug}` },
      ],
    })}
  </script>
  <!-- FAQPage structured data for rich results -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />

  <div class="budgeting-hero-with-image">
    <AngleHero
      title="Budgeting App & Expense Tracking"
      subtitle="Track spending, manage monthly expenses, and see where your money goes. Zero-based budgeting with real-time cashflow analysis."
      keyword="budget & expense tracker"
    />

    <div class="w-full overflow-x-clip -mt-56 md:-mt-[23rem] mb-0 relative z-0 flex justify-center">
    <div class="hero-image-reveal w-max max-w-full min-w-0 shrink-0">
      <div class="scale-[1.15] md:scale-100 origin-center md:w-[960px] md:max-w-none">
        <img
          src="/images/budgeting-app/hero_light.png"
          alt={meta.title}
          class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block dark:hidden"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/budgeting-app/hero_dark.png"
          alt={meta.title}
          class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block hidden dark:block"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: What it is -->
  <Section
    heading="Track Spending, Manage Cashflow, Master Your Budget"
    bg="stone"
    align="center"
    class="mt-4 md:mt-0 !pt-12 md:!pt-2"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        Finzen is a budgeting app that teaches you to <strong>track every dollar with intention</strong>. Built around zero-based budgeting, where every dollar has a job. It turns expense tracking from a chore into a 3-minute daily habit that puts you in the driver's seat. Whether you need a budget to stop living paycheck to paycheck or you're ready to <strong>level up your spending plan</strong>, you'll learn exactly where your money goes, how to organize it across spending categories, and how to use cash flow analysis to stay ahead instead of reacting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 2: Zero-Based Budgeting -->
  <Section
    heading="Zero-Based Budgeting: Give every dollar a job"
    align="center"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-8">
      <!-- Image between title and first paragraph (animate in from below when in view). Padding gives drop shadow room. -->
      <div class="budget-envelope-reveal flex justify-center pt-4 pb-9 px-4 -mb-1">
        <img
          src="/images/budgeting-app/budget_envelope.png"
          alt="Envelope budgeting: allocate dollars to categories"
          class="w-full max-w-[200px] h-auto drop-shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] dark:drop-shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.4)]"
        />
      </div>

      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">Zero-based budgeting</strong> means every dollar has a job - unlike tracking after you spend, you decide where money goes at the start of the month. It's the same idea as the classic envelope budget system: you allocate cash to envelopes (groceries, rent, fun) and when an envelope is empty, you stop or move money intentionally. Finzen brings that discipline into a <strong class="text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">digital cash envelope budgeting</strong> experience: allocate, spend down, and always see what      </p>

      <!-- 3-step diagram between the two paragraphs -->
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center pt-4 pb-0 -mb-4" aria-label="Budget cycle: Plan your month, Track your spending, Adjust your plan">
        <div class="relative w-full max-w-[420px] aspect-square">
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full text-neutral-300 dark:text-neutral-600" viewBox="0 0 400 400" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <marker id="cycle-arrowhead" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="7" refY="3" orient="auto">
                <polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="currentColor" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path d="M 321.2 130 A 140 140 0 1 1 78.8 130" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrowhead)" />
            <path d="M 78.8 130 A 140 140 0 1 1 200 340" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrowhead)" />
            <path d="M 200 340 A 140 140 0 1 1 321.2 130" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrowhead)" />
          </svg>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-[21%] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
            <div class="w-16 h-16 sm:w-[4.5rem] sm:h-[4.5rem] rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 ring-2 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-neutral-700 shadow-sm flex-shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-8 h-8 sm:w-9 sm:h-9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 text-center max-w-[5rem]">Plan your month</span>
          </div>
          <div class="absolute left-[80.3%] top-[67.5%] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
            <div class="w-16 h-16 sm:w-[4.5rem] sm:h-[4.5rem] rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 ring-2 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-neutral-700 shadow-sm flex-shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-8 h-8 sm:w-9 sm:h-9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-3 7h3m-3 4h3m-6-4h.01M9 16h.01" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 text-center max-w-[5.5rem]">Track your spending</span>
          </div>
          <div class="absolute left-[19.7%] top-[67.5%] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
            <div class="w-16 h-16 sm:w-[4.5rem] sm:h-[4.5rem] rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 ring-2 ring-neutral-200 dark:ring-neutral-700 shadow-sm flex-shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-8 h-8 sm:w-9 sm:h-9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 text-center max-w-[5.5rem]">Adjust your plan</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        At the start of each month, use Finzen's <strong class="text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">budget planner</strong> to assign your income across spending categories until you hit zero unassigned dollars. As you track spending, each category shows exactly what's left, so you always know if you can afford something or need to pull from another envelope. This is how you finally answer <strong class="text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">where does my money go</strong> in real time instead of at month's end. Category budgeting replaces a static monthly budget template with a <strong class="text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">live spending plan</strong> that keeps you intentional instead of reactive.
      </p>

      <!-- Budget bars: spent / budget; animate filling on scroll into view -->
      <div class="budget-bars-container max-w-xl mx-auto">
        <div class="space-y-3 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 p-4 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900/50">
          <div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-1">
              <span>Groceries</span>
              <span>$510 / $600</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2 rounded-full bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 overflow-hidden">
              <div class="budget-bar-fill bar-fill-85 h-full rounded-full bg-emerald-500/80 dark:bg-emerald-500/70"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-1">
              <span>Dining &amp; coffee</span>
              <span>$120 / $200</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2 rounded-full bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 overflow-hidden">
              <div class="budget-bar-fill bar-fill-60 h-full rounded-full bg-amber-500/80 dark:bg-amber-500/70"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-1">
              <span>Transport</span>
              <span>$150 / $150</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2 rounded-full bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 overflow-hidden">
              <div class="budget-bar-fill bar-fill-100 h-full rounded-full bg-blue-500/80 dark:bg-blue-500/70"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-1">
              <span>Subscriptions</span>
              <span>$36 / $80</span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2 rounded-full bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 overflow-hidden">
              <div class="budget-bar-fill bar-fill-45 h-full rounded-full bg-violet-500/80 dark:bg-violet-500/70"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 3: Spending Categories -->
  <Section
    heading="Flexible categories that fit your life"
    bg="stone"
    align="center"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-left">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Custom Categories', detail: 'Create spending categories that match how you actually spend — not a one-size-fits-all list.', icon: '<path d="M9 2l5 5-7 7H2v-4l7-7z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>' },
          { label: 'Starter Templates', detail: 'Pre-built category sets for common budgeting styles so you can start in minutes, then tweak.', icon: '<circle cx="8" cy="6" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" fill="none"/><path d="M6 10v2.5h4V10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>' },
          { label: 'Subcategories', detail: 'Break down broad buckets like Food into Groceries, Dining Out, and Coffee for clearer tracking.', icon: '<path d="M4 13V7M8 13V4M12 13V2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>' },
          { label: 'Category Budgets', detail: 'Set a monthly limit per category and see at a glance how much is left as you spend.', icon: '<path d="M2 4L8 8L14 4M14 4V12H2V4H14Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Expense tracking: budget view, spending trends, spending donut -->
  <Section
    heading="Expense Tracking That Builds Money Awareness"
    bg="stone"
    align="center"
    class="!bg-gradient-to-b !from-white !to-[#ECECEC] dark:!bg-gradient-to-t dark:!from-[#1B1B1B] dark:!to-[#171717]"
  >
    <!-- 3 screenshots left to right: budget view, spending trends, spending donut (light/dark by mode) -->
    <div class="screenshot-pile flex justify-center items-end mb-12 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-2 sm:px-4 overflow-visible min-h-[160px] sm:min-h-[180px] md:min-h-[220px] max-sm:mt-6 -mt-12 md:-mt-6">
      <div class="screenshot-in-left screenshot-card w-[154px] sm:w-[220px] md:w-[330px] aspect-[700/543] rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-[0_20px_40px_-8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15),0_32px_80px_-16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.2)] dark:shadow-[0_24px_48px_-12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.45)] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-600/50 flex-shrink-0 -mr-12 sm:-mr-16 md:-mr-12 z-0">
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/budget_view_light.png" alt="Budget view" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover block dark:hidden" />
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/budget_view_dark.png" alt="Budget view" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover hidden dark:block" />
      </div>
      <div class="screenshot-in-bottom screenshot-card w-[200px] sm:w-[260px] md:w-[390px] aspect-[700/543] rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-[0_20px_40px_-8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15),0_32px_80px_-16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.2)] dark:shadow-[0_24px_48px_-12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.45)] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-600/50 flex-shrink-0 -mr-12 sm:-mr-16 md:-mr-12 mt-6 sm:mt-8 md:mt-10 z-10">
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/spending_trends_light.png" alt="Spending trends" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover block dark:hidden" />
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/spending_trends_dark.png" alt="Spending trends" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover hidden dark:block" />
      </div>
      <div class="screenshot-in-right screenshot-card w-[154px] sm:w-[220px] md:w-[330px] aspect-[700/543] rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-[0_20px_40px_-8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15),0_32px_80px_-16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.2)] dark:shadow-[0_24px_48px_-12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.45)] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-600/50 flex-shrink-0 z-0">
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/spending_donut_light.png" alt="Spending by category (donut)" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover block dark:hidden" />
        <img src="/images/budgeting-app/spending_donut_dark.png" alt="Spending by category (donut)" width="700" height="543" class="screenshot-card-img w-full h-full object-cover hidden dark:block" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <style>
      @keyframes slideInLeft {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(-80px) rotate(-8deg); }
        to { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0) rotate(-6deg); }
      }
      @keyframes slideInBottom {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(60px) rotate(0deg); }
        to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) rotate(2deg); }
      }
      @keyframes slideInRight {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(80px) rotate(8deg); }
        to { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0) rotate(6deg); }
      }
      .screenshot-pile .screenshot-in-left {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateX(-80px) rotate(-8deg);
      }
      .screenshot-pile .screenshot-in-bottom {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(60px) rotate(0deg);
      }
      .screenshot-pile .screenshot-in-right {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateX(80px) rotate(8deg);
      }
      .screenshot-pile.in-view .screenshot-in-left {
        animation: slideInLeft 0.7s ease-out forwards;
      }
      .screenshot-pile.in-view .screenshot-in-bottom {
        animation: slideInBottom 0.7s ease-out 0.15s forwards;
      }
      .screenshot-pile.in-view .screenshot-in-right {
        animation: slideInRight 0.7s ease-out 0.3s forwards;
      }
      /* Crisp rendering: avoid blur from rotated card compositing and non-integer scaling */
      .screenshot-card-img {
        transform: translateZ(0);
        backface-visibility: hidden;
      }
    </style>

    <script>
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        const pile = document.querySelectorAll('.screenshot-pile');
        pile.forEach((p) => {
          const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
            (entries) => {
              entries.forEach((entry) => {
                if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                  entry.target.classList.add('in-view');
                }
              });
            },
            { rootMargin: '0px 0px -80px 0px', threshold: 0.1 }
          );
          observer.observe(p);
        });
      });
    </script>

    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        The real power comes from watching your patterns evolve. Finzen breaks down your spending habits through category comparisons, monthly trends, and visual reports that show exactly where your money goes. You start competing with last month's version of yourself: can you shave $50 off dining out? Keep groceries under budget three months in a row?
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-bold">
        Finzen turns expense tracking into a game you actually want to win, and the scoreboard updates every time you log a transaction.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-6 flex justify-center">
        <a
          href={APP_URL}
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-7 py-3.5 bg-[#0a0a0a] text-white text-base font-medium rounded-xl hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-[0_10px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.2)] dark:bg-white dark:text-[#1B1B1B] dark:hover:-translate-y-1 dark:hover:shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(0,0,0,0.65)] transition-all duration-200 shadow-sm"
        >
          Try Finzen free
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Habits that make the budget stick (budget/expense-tracking angle) -->
  <Section
    heading="Habits that make your budget stick"
    align="center"
  >
    <div class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 md:gap-6">
      <!-- Card 1: Pause before you spend -->
      <div class="habit-card rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 transition-transform duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-[8px_8px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08),-4px_-4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[8px_8px_18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),10px_10px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12),-3px_-3px_6px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="6" y="4" width="4" height="16" rx="1"/>
            <rect x="14" y="4" width="4" height="16" rx="1"/>
