            <span itemprop="name">How can I stop overspending on things I don't really need?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon flex-shrink-0 w-4 h-4 text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </button>
        </dt>
        <dd id="faq-answer-1" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner pb-6 pt-0" itemprop="text">
            <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
              The trick is catching overspending before it becomes a pattern. Set category limits that reflect what you actually want to spend, not what you think you should spend. When you see your dining-out category at €180/€200 by the 20th of the month, that visual feedback creates a natural pause. Track spending as it happens so you know what's left, and suddenly that impulse purchase competes with your other priorities. Financial awareness is what changes spending habits.
            </p>
          </div>
        </dd>
      </div>

