            <span itemprop="name">Can budgeting help if I'm living paycheck to paycheck?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon flex-shrink-0 w-4 h-4 text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </button>
        </dt>
        <dd id="faq-answer-4" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner pb-6 pt-0" itemprop="text">
            <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
              Yes. Zero-based budgeting works especially well when money is tight because every dollar gets a specific job before you spend it. Start by budgeting what you have right now, not what you hope to earn next month. Assign money to must-pay bills first, then essentials, then whatever's left. Envelope budgeting shows you exactly what's available without touching money that's already allocated. Seeing your cashflow clearly is often the first step to breaking the cycle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div
        class="faq-item border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800"
        itemscope
        itemprop="mainEntity"
        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
      >
        <dt class="faq-question">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="faq-trigger w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-left py-5 text-base font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 transition-colors"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="faq-answer-5"
            id="faq-question-5"
          >
            <span itemprop="name">Do I really need a budget if I'm not struggling with money?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon flex-shrink-0 w-4 h-4 text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </button>
        </dt>
        <dd id="faq-answer-5" class="faq-answer" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner pb-6 pt-0" itemprop="text">
            <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
              Even if you're not in financial trouble, a budget shows you opportunities you're missing. Where could you cut €100/month without noticing? Which spending categories are creeping up? How much could you actually save or invest if you were intentional? A spending plan isn't about fixing problems—it's about optimizing what's already working. People with healthy finances often benefit most from budget management because they have room to make strategic choices. Tracking monthly spending turns vague financial goals into concrete actions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <script>
      (function () {
        const accordion = document.querySelector('.faq-accordion');
        if (!accordion) return;
        const items = accordion.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');
        const openClass = 'faq-item-open';

        function closeAll() {
          items.forEach((item) => {
            item.classList.remove(openClass);
            const btn = item.querySelector('.faq-trigger');
            if (btn) btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
          });
        }

        function openItem(item) {
          closeAll();
          item.classList.add(openClass);
          const btn = item.querySelector('.faq-trigger');
          if (btn) btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        }

        function toggleItem(item) {
          const isOpen = item.classList.contains(openClass);
          if (isOpen) closeAll();
          else openItem(item);
        }

        items.forEach((item) => {
          const btn = item.querySelector('.faq-trigger');
          if (!btn) return;
          btn.addEventListener('click', () => toggleItem(item));
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </Section>

  <CTABlock
    heading="Take Control of Your Money"
